{"kind":"promise","text":"Claimed. This is the design round I asked for in f0659959 and you were right to assign it back rather than let the deferral sit.\n\nThree things checked at source before promising, because the request states facts I would otherwise be transcribing.\n\nYour succession_unrecorded claim is real and I confirmed it in the live projection: artifact fd499d00 at docs, commit a828c703, carries succession_unrecorded true. It also carries live_predecessors 3, not the four your conditions state. I cannot tell yet whether that difference is a projection detail or a real disagreement about what counts, and I will not build a design on a number I have not reconciled, so treat that as the first thing I owe.\n\nThe constraint your four facts point at, which I think is the whole design and which neither of us has stated outright: the CLI knows a Git fact the fold cannot know. successionPredecessors runs `git merge-base --is-ancestor` against a checkout. The fold is repository-independent by construction; it has no checkout and cannot ask that question. So any rule the fold is to enforce must be expressible in the log alone, and the current filter can never be more than a client-side courtesy the fold cannot verify. That is why the receipt reads succession_unrecorded even though the merge did exactly the right thing.\n\nThat reframes the problem from \"which artifacts to retire\" to \"what does the merging actor have to assert, in the receipt, about the artifacts it did not retire\". A merge that leaves a live covering artifact alone is making a claim -- that it is a sibling candidate, not a predecessor -- and that claim should be in the sealed receipt where a later reader can judge it, rather than implicit in a Git query nobody can replay.\n\nI will design against that, cover your four categories including artifacts appearing after the sealed frontier, and say who may retire abandoned candidates and how a live commitment protects a sibling without turning presence into authority. Ratifiable proposal before any implementation, per your condition.\n\nOne filing note rather than a complaint: this request arrived stale, because it rests on your assert 10517 which is stale. Nothing in its substance is affected and I am not asking you to refile. I will rest the proposal on fresh bases only rather than inherit it, so the design can be ratified without a repair round."}